.SH DESCRIPTION
When invoked, 
.B barry
will compile the specified sources into an executable file
.B run
through a series of translation phases. The various options can be used to control the printing of intermediate forms and to control which optimizations are performed. If source files are organised in ML Basis Files (files with extension .mlb), the compiler will memoize symbol table information and object code in the dedicated MLB directories located relative to the source files.

If barry is invoked without source files, an interactive REPL is started. Type ':help;' within the REPL to learn more about its use.

To learn more about programming with MLKit, consult the MLKit web page at

.B http://melsman.github.io/mlkit
.SH STANDARDS
The MLKit implements Standard ML (Revised 1997) and has almost full support for the Standard ML Basis Library (version of 2002). See the MLKit home page for a detailed overview of the support for the Standard ML Basis Library.
.SH EXAMPLES
For examples, consult the MLKit manual "Programming with Regions in the MLKit", which is available from the MLKit home page.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP "\fB--SML_LIB S\fR" 4
.IX Item "--SML_LIB S"
Installation directory for the MLKit standard library.
For normal execution you should not modify this value.
However, if you wish to use the MLKit with an altered
runtime system you can update this setting and the
system will try to link to a runtime system found in
the specified install directory.
.IP "\fB--aggressive_opt, -aopt\fR" 4
.IX Item "--aggressive_opt, -aopt"
Enable aggressive optimisations, including aggressive
inlining. These optimisations are not guaranteed to be
region safe. Turning off garbage collection automatically
turns off this option.
.IP "\fB--chat, -verbose\fR" 4
.IX Item "--chat, -verbose"
Print a message for each compilation step in the compiler.
.IP "\fB--compile_only, -c\fR" 4
.IX Item "--compile_only, -c"
Compile only. Suppresses generation of executable
.IP "\fB--compiler_timings, -timings\fR" 4
.IX Item "--compiler_timings, -timings"
Show compiler timings for each compilation phase.
.IP "\fB--constant_folding, -cfold\fR" 4
.IX Item "--constant_folding, -cfold"
Enable constant folding optimisations.
.IP "\fB--contract\fR" 4
.IX Item "--contract"
Contract is responsible for inlining, specialization,
elimination of dead code, and much else (Lambda
Expression Optimiser).
.IP "\fB--cross_module_opt, -cross_opt\fR" 4
.IX Item "--cross_module_opt, -cross_opt"
Enable cross-module optimisation including inlining
of small functions and specialisation of small
recursive functions. Which optimisations are performed
across modules is controlled by individual optimisation
flags.
.IP "\fB--debug_compiler, -debug\fR" 4
.IX Item "--debug_compiler, -debug"
Print intermediate forms of a program during compilation.
.IP "\fB--debug_linking\fR" 4
.IX Item "--debug_linking"
Debug linking of target code by showing which object
files are linked together.
.IP "\fB--debug_man_enrich\fR" 4
.IX Item "--debug_man_enrich"
Show information about why a program unit need be
recompiled. A program unit (or a functor body)
is recompiled if either (a) the program unit is
modified, or (b) information about an identifier
for which the program unit depends upon has changed.
.IP "\fB--drop_unused_funargs, -dufa\fR" 4
.IX Item "--drop_unused_funargs, -dufa"
Drop function arguments that are unused.
.IP "\fB--eliminate_explicit_records\fR" 4
.IX Item "--eliminate_explicit_records"
Eliminate bindings of explicit records only used for
selections. Transform
      let r = (e1,...,en) in ... #i r .. #j r ...
into
      let x1=e1 in ... let xn=en in ... xi .. xj ...
(Lambda Expression Optimiser).
.IP "\fB--eliminate_polymorphic_equality\fR" 4
.IX Item "--eliminate_polymorphic_equality"
Replace polymorphic equality with equality functions
generated for the types at which it is used; a function
that compares values of an equality type variable is
given an extra argument for each such variable. Barry
turns this option off, so that its output uses the =
operator, but a backend that has no polymorphic equality
of its own wants it on.
.IP "\fB--fix_floating\fR" 4
.IX Item "--fix_floating"
Float fix-bindings into immediate let-bindings when
possible to help tail-calls not be captured in let-
region bindings.
.IP "\fB--help\fR" 4
.IX Item "--help"
Print extended help information and exit.
.IP "\fB--help S\fR" 4
.IX Item "--help S"
Print help information about an option and exit.
.IP "\fB--import_basislib, -basislib\fR" 4
.IX Item "--import_basislib, -basislib"
Import Basis Library automatically in your projects. If 
you wish to make use of the Standard ML Basis Library
in your projects, this option should be turned on, unless
you wish to import the Basis Library manually in your
projects.
.IP "\fB--inline_functors\fR" 4
.IX Item "--inline_functors"
Inline functors during static interpretation instead of
generating separate target code blocks for functor bodies
and arguments. With the flag enabled, performance may
increase with the cost of larger (re)compilation times.
The flag may be controlled in mlb-files using mlb-
annotations.
.IP "\fB--inline_names S\fR" 4
.IX Item "--inline_names S"
Names of functions that should always be inlined
if possible, no matter the setting of the flag
--maximum_inline_size.
.IP "\fB--link_code S\fR" 4
.IX Item "--link_code S"
Link-files to be linked together to form an
executable.
.IP "\fB--link_time_dead_code_elimination, -ltdce\fR" 4
.IX Item "--link_time_dead_code_elimination, -ltdce"
Link time dead code elimination.
.IP "\fB--load_basis_files S, -load S\fR" 4
.IX Item "--load_basis_files S, -load S"
Basis files to be loaded before compilation
proper.
.IP "\fB--log_to_file\fR" 4
.IX Item "--log_to_file"
Log to files instead of stdout.
.IP "\fB--man\fR" 4
.IX Item "--man"
Print man-page and exit.
.IP "\fB--maximum_inline_size N, -max_inl_sz N\fR" 4
.IX Item "--maximum_inline_size N, -max_inl_sz N"
Functions smaller than this size (counted in abstract
syntax tree nodes) are inlined, even if they are used
more than once. Functions that are used only once are
always inlined. A function declared in one program unit
may be inlined when applied in another program unit
provided the function is sufficiently closed (refers only
to exported identifiers) and provided the option
--cross_opt is enabled.
.IP "\fB--maximum_specialise_size N, -max_spec_sz N\fR" 4
.IX Item "--maximum_specialise_size N, -max_spec_sz N"
Function-parameterised functions smaller than this size
(counted in abstract syntax tree nodes) are specialised if
all applications of the function within its own body are
applied to its formal function argument, even if they are used
more than once. Functions that are used only once are
specialised no matter their size. A function declared in
one program unit may be specialised when applied in
another program unit provided the function is sufficiently
closed (refers only to exported identifiers) and provided
the option --cross_opt is enabled. See also the option
--specialize_recursive_functions.
.IP "\fB--messages\fR" 4
.IX Item "--messages"
Print messages about reading source files and generating
target files.
.IP "\fB--minimize_fixs\fR" 4
.IX Item "--minimize_fixs"
Minimize fix constructs (Lambda Expression Optimiser).
.IP "\fB--mlb_path_maps S, -mlb-path-map S\fR" 4
.IX Item "--mlb_path_maps S, -mlb-path-map S"
ML Basis path map files to be used.
.IP "\fB--namebase S\fR" 4
.IX Item "--namebase S"
Name base to enforce unique names when compiling
mlb-files.
.IP "\fB--no_aggressive_opt, -no_aopt\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_aggressive_opt, -no_aopt"
Opposite of --aggressive_opt, -aopt.
.IP "\fB--no_constant_folding, -no_cfold\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_constant_folding, -no_cfold"
Opposite of --constant_folding, -cfold.
.IP "\fB--no_contract\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_contract"
Opposite of --contract.
.IP "\fB--no_cross_module_opt, -no_cross_opt\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_cross_module_opt, -no_cross_opt"
Opposite of --cross_module_opt, -cross_opt.
.IP "\fB--no_drop_unused_funargs, -no_dufa\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_drop_unused_funargs, -no_dufa"
Opposite of --drop_unused_funargs, -dufa.
.IP "\fB--no_eliminate_explicit_records\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_eliminate_explicit_records"
Opposite of --eliminate_explicit_records.
.IP "\fB--no_eliminate_polymorphic_equality\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_eliminate_polymorphic_equality"
Opposite of --eliminate_polymorphic_equality.
.IP "\fB--no_fix_floating\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_fix_floating"
Opposite of --fix_floating.
.IP "\fB--no_import_basislib, -no_basislib\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_import_basislib, -no_basislib"
Opposite of --import_basislib, -basislib.
.IP "\fB--no_link_time_dead_code_elimination, -no_ltdce\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_link_time_dead_code_elimination, -no_ltdce"
Opposite of --link_time_dead_code_elimination, -ltdce.
.IP "\fB--no_messages\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_messages"
Opposite of --messages.
.IP "\fB--no_minimize_fixs\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_minimize_fixs"
Opposite of --minimize_fixs.
.IP "\fB--no_optimiser, -no_opt\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_optimiser, -no_opt"
Opposite of --optimiser, -opt.
.IP "\fB--no_raggedRight\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_raggedRight"
Opposite of --raggedRight.
.IP "\fB--no_specialize_recursive_functions\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_specialize_recursive_functions"
Opposite of --specialize_recursive_functions.
.IP "\fB--no_type_check_lambda\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_type_check_lambda"
Opposite of --type_check_lambda.
.IP "\fB--no_unbox_funargs\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_unbox_funargs"
Opposite of --unbox_funargs.
.IP "\fB--no_uncurrying, -no_uncurry\fR" 4
.IX Item "--no_uncurrying, -no_uncurry"
Opposite of --uncurrying, -uncurry.
.IP "\fB--optimiser, -opt\fR" 4
.IX Item "--optimiser, -opt"
Enable optimisation of intermediate language code
(Lambda Expressions). Which optimisations are performed
is controlled by individual flags. The optimisations
include function inlining, function specialisation,
fix-minimization, unboxing of function arguments, and
elimination of unnecessary record constructions.
.IP "\fB--output S, -o S\fR" 4
.IX Item "--output S, -o S"
The name of the executable file generated by
the Kit.
.IP "\fB--parallel_compilation N, -j N\fR" 4
.IX Item "--parallel_compilation N, -j N"
The maximum number of parallel processes used
for compilation.
.IP "\fB--pretty_depth N\fR" 4
.IX Item "--pretty_depth N"
This flag controls the pretty-printing depth of
values printed in the REPL. The value must be an
integer larger than zero.
.IP "\fB--pretty_string_size N\fR" 4
.IX Item "--pretty_string_size N"
This flag controls the pretty-printing size of
strings printed in the REPL. The value must be an
integer larger than zero.
.IP "\fB--print_closed_export_bases, -Pceb\fR" 4
.IX Item "--print_closed_export_bases, -Pceb"
Controls printing of closed export bases.
.IP "\fB--print_excon_name\fR" 4
.IX Item "--print_excon_name"
Print underlying unique name when printing excons.
.IP "\fB--print_export_bases, -Peb\fR" 4
.IX Item "--print_export_bases, -Peb"
Controls printing of export bases.
.IP "\fB--print_lvar_name\fR" 4
.IX Item "--print_lvar_name"
Print underlying unique name when printing lvars.
.IP "\fB--print_opt_lambda_expression, -Pole\fR" 4
.IX Item "--print_opt_lambda_expression, -Pole"
Print Lambda Expression after optimisation.
.IP "\fB--print_post_elab_ast, -Ppeast\fR" 4
.IX Item "--print_post_elab_ast, -Ppeast"
Print ast after elaboration.
.IP "\fB--print_type_name_stamps, -Ptypestamps\fR" 4
.IX Item "--print_type_name_stamps, -Ptypestamps"
Print type name stamps and their attributes in types
and expressions.
.IP "\fB--print_types, -Ptypes\fR" 4
.IX Item "--print_types, -Ptypes"
Print types when printing intermediate forms. For Lambda
Expressions, ordinary ML types are printed, whereas for
Region Expressions, region types are printed.
.IP "\fB--quotation, -quot\fR" 4
.IX Item "--quotation, -quot"
Enable support for quotations and anti-quotations.
When enabled, the datatype
   datatype 'a frag = QUOTE of string
                    | ANTIQUOTE 'a
is available in the initial environment. Moreover,
values of this datatype may be constructed using
the quotation/antiquotation syntax:
   val s = "world" 
   val a : string frag list = `hello ^s - goodbye`
.IP "\fB--raggedRight\fR" 4
.IX Item "--raggedRight"
Use ragged right margin in pretty-printing of
expressions and types.
.IP "\fB--recompile_basislib, -scratch\fR" 4
.IX Item "--recompile_basislib, -scratch"
Recompile basis library from scratch. This option
is useful together with other options that control
code generation.
.IP "\fB--report_file_sig, -sig\fR" 4
.IX Item "--report_file_sig, -sig"
Report signatures for each file read.
.IP "\fB--safeLinkTimeElimination\fR" 4
.IX Item "--safeLinkTimeElimination"
Treat this module as a library in the sense that
the code can be eliminated if it is not used,
even if the code has side effects.
.IP "\fB--specialize_recursive_functions\fR" 4
.IX Item "--specialize_recursive_functions"
Specialise recursive functions. Use the option
maximum_specialise_size to control which functions
are specialised. If this flag is on, functions that are
applied only once are specialised, no matter the setting
of --maximum_specialise_size (Lambda Expression Optimiser).
.IP "\fB--statistics_after_optimisation, -stats_opt\fR" 4
.IX Item "--statistics_after_optimisation, -stats_opt"
Report optimisation statistics after optimisation of
Lambda Expression.
.IP "\fB--type_check_lambda\fR" 4
.IX Item "--type_check_lambda"
Type check lambda expression prior to performing region
inference. Type checking is very fast and for normal use
you should not disable this option. Type checking
intermediate forms is very powerful for eliminating bugs
in the compiler.
.IP "\fB--unbox_funargs\fR" 4
.IX Item "--unbox_funargs"
Unbox arguments to fix-bound functions, for which the
argument 'a' is used only in contexts '#i a'. All call 
sites are transformed to match the new function (Lambda
Expression Optimiser).
.IP "\fB--uncurrying, -uncurry\fR" 4
.IX Item "--uncurrying, -uncurry"
Enable uncurrying of curried functions. The uncurried
function takes its arguments unboxed in registers or
on the stack. For partial applications and non-
application uses of the function, appropriate eta-
expansions are applied.
.IP "\fB--version, -v, -V\fR" 4
.IX Item "--version, -v, -V"
Print version information and exit.
.IP "\fB--width N, -w N\fR" 4
.IX Item "--width N, -w N"
Column width used when pretty printing intermediate code.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits with status 0 on success and -1 on failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
A library install directory must be provided in an environment variable SML_LIB, as a path-definition in the user's personal path-map ~/.barry/mlb-path-map, or in a system wide path-map /home/skye/Research/3cps/mlkit-frontend/vendor/mlkit/../mlkit-install/etc/barry/mlb-path-map.
.SH FILES
.IP /home/skye/Research/3cps/mlkit-frontend/vendor/mlkit/../mlkit-install/etc/barry/mlb-path-map
System-wide configuration of library and runtime system locations
.IP ~/.barry/mlb-path-map
User specific configuration of library and runtime system locations
